#!/usr/bin/env bash
#
# glossary-post-body — print the canonical body of a language's pinned forum
# glossary post to stdout. It writes nothing and touches nothing.
#
# Usage:
#   ./scripts/glossary-post-body <lang>
#
# Example:
#   ./scripts/glossary-post-body pt-BR
#
# The body is a pointer, not a copy of the table. A full glossary runs to 100+
# rows, which is unreadable in a forum post (especially on a phone) and goes out
# of date the moment we agree a term. The live version lives on the review site
# at https://i18n.jiki.io/<lang>/glossary, where each section has its own anchor,
# so a reply can link a section and quote a row rather than the whole table.
#
# That page is generated by ./scripts/publish-glossary and only exists once
# i18n-site has been deployed, so publish and deploy before any post carrying
# this body goes up or gets refreshed, or the link lands on nothing.
#
# This is the one home for the wording. Both consumers shell out to it:
#   - scripts/create-forum-glossary-post   (first post for a new language)
#   - /update-guide-and-glossary           (refresh after an agreed change)
# Because the body is identical for every language bar the name and the URL, a
# refresh is a re-print of this, never a rebuild from glossary.md.
#
# Reads:   languages/names.json
# Requires: jq.

set -euo pipefail

die() { echo "error: $*" >&2; exit 1; }

command -v jq >/dev/null || die "jq is required"

LANG_CODE="${1:-}"
[ -n "$LANG_CODE" ] || die "usage: $(basename "$0") <lang>"

ROOT="$(cd "$(dirname "$0")/.." && pwd)"
NAMES="$ROOT/languages/names.json"

[ -f "$NAMES" ] || die "names file not found: $NAMES"

LANG_NAME="$(jq -r --arg l "$LANG_CODE" '.[$l] // empty' "$NAMES")"
[ -n "$LANG_NAME" ] || die "locale '$LANG_CODE' not found in $NAMES — add it before running this script"

SITE_URL="https://i18n.jiki.io/${LANG_CODE}/glossary/"

cat << ENDOFBODY
One of the most crucial steps in translating Jiki is determining the right terms to consistently use throughout. Generally these are technical terms, or terms used in the Jiki analogies. This is a thread, intended to go on forever, where we can highlight incorrect terms and agree correct variants.

The current ${LANG_NAME} glossary lives here:

${SITE_URL}

That page is always the live version: we update it as soon as we agree a change here, so it is the one to check rather than anything quoted further down this thread.

When something is wrong, quote the row here (copy the term and what we render it as) and tell us what it should be instead. That way we know exactly which decision you are giving feedback on.

---

Please use this thread to discuss any changes or additions you think should be made. **Please do NOT use LLMs to generate suggestions and only use your own personal knowledge**.
ENDOFBODY
